##Version 1
Started out as a simnple n8n workflow. I had no webhooks yet, no backened proxy, no summary histroy and no frontend. 
But then I thought I could make this a real user experience.

---
##Version 2
- Added webhook into workflow.
- Created simple but aesthetic UI frontend within Lovable.
- I ran into a CORS issue so I added Supabase as a backened proxy.
- Got Lovable to add 'open google doc' button, so the user can open it into a new tab.
- Also used Supabase to log each summary history. Holds URL, Id, summary and date.

---
##Version 3
- I tried to add a way for users to have full ownership and accessibility to any docs made. Since each doc was being created in my Google Drive account.
- Tried solving this with Google log-in, but I just could not because of an authentication problem from my side.
- So I tried email log-in, but the magic link from Supabase wouldn't bring me back to the main UI in Lovable. I could have found another solution admittably.
- I want to come back to this plan to make the tool feel like a complete user experiwnce, allowing them to have full ownership. On top of this, I will add email intergration so the docs can be shared easily to another person or team.
